        "pareto_vs_deployment_clarification": "On the unconstrained mathematical Pareto frontier across (val MAE, Latency, Size), LSTM Compact (val MAE 41.181, latency 0.0098 ms, size 0.048 MB) and Linear Regression (val MAE 46.852, 0.0152 ms, 0.003 MB) strictly dominate XGBoost_Fast. Consequently, XGBoost_Fast is not on the unconstrained validation Pareto frontier. However, XGBoost_Fast (50 trees, depth 5, lr 0.12, val MAE 41.349, test MAE 66.0738, test R2 0.2121) was selected as an operationally constrained deployment model. This constraint is necessitated by production system requirements: (1) native C++ TreeSHAP feature attributions require tree structures, (2) calibrated normalized conformal uncertainty quantification is empirically fitted and validated for tree-based dispersion, and (3) a unified tree runtime avoids managing mixed deep-learning and tree dependencies in latency-sensitive serving environments."
      }
